  "query_preview": "..\n(Tonight through next Friday)\nIssued at 1031 PM CDT Fri Aug 14 2026\n\n00Z upper air analysis places a 598 dm high over Louisiana and\nsouthern Mississippi. This upper-level high is responsible for\nthe very hot temperatures and mainly dry weather thus far across \nthe Mid-South. Late evening temperatures remain uncomfortable and \nvery warm in the 80s across the area with surface dewpoints in the\n70s, resulting in heat index values in the 90s.\n\nThe aforementioned upper-level ridge is expected to remain in\nplace across the Lower Mississippi Valley this weekend resulting\nin a continuation of dangerously hot temperatures across the\narea. Latest guidance suggests slightly lower dewpoints,\nespecially across areas along and west of the Mississippi River.\nThese lower dewpoints will likely translate to higher\ntemperatures at or above 100 degrees with heat index values\napproaching or exceeding 110 degrees in many locations,\nespecially on Sunday. Regardless, the combination of very hot and\nhumid conditions combined with successive days of dangerous heat\nand little to no relief at night will result in the Extreme Heat\nWarning remaining in effect through Sunday evening. Probabilities\nremain very low (<10% chance) for any convective development into\nSunday.\n\nMid to long range model trends continue to indicate the upper-\nlevel ridge axis retrograding into the Southern Plains by next\nweek. This will allow for a weak front to drop into the Lower\nMississippi Valley with low chances (isolated/scattered coverage)\nfor showers and thunderstorms each day during peak heating as\noverall shear will remain weak, favoring pulse-type convection.\nAdditional heat headlines look likely well into next week with\ncoverage depending on where the front stalls out across the Mid-\nSouth. NAEFS/EPS data suggests some relief in the form of\nslightly lower temperatures and an uptick in rain chances may be\nin store for late next week into the following weekend with lower\nmid-level heights across the eastern U.S.",
